{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":530},{"id":2,"videos":3,"agency":6,"agency_full":7,"sector":8,"dest":9,"color":10,"year":11,"status":12,"departure_date":13,"arrival_date":14,"transit_days":15,"vehicle":16,"payload":17,"delta_v":18,"data_quality":19,"credit":20,"links":21,"flight_data_quality":37,"fleet_refs":38,"flight":44,"name":499,"type":500,"first":501,"dispatch":502,"description":503,"events":504,"vehicle_stage":46},"perseverance",[4],{"id":5},"vid-54cee894b509","NASA","National Aeronautics and Space Administration / Jet Propulsion Laboratory","gov","MARS","#0B3D91",2020,"ACTIVE","2020-07-30","2021-02-18",203,"Atlas V 541","about 4060 kg launch mass (1025 kg rover; 1.8 kg Ingenuity helicopter)","~6.1 km/s","good","© NASA / JPL-Caltech — U.S. Government work, public domain. First helicopter on another planet (Ingenuity, retired 2024-01). Cached samples in tubes; the NASA-ESA Mars Sample Return that was to retrieve them was cancelled in 2026.",[22,26,29,33],{"l":23,"u":24,"t":25},"Perseverance (rover) — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perseverance_(rover)","intro",{"l":27,"u":28,"t":25},"Mars 2020 (NASA)","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/",{"l":30,"u":31,"t":32},"Ingenuity helicopter — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingenuity_(helicopter)","core",{"l":34,"u":35,"t":36},"Mars Sample Return architecture","https://mars.nasa.gov/msr/","deep","measured",[39,42],{"id":40,"role":41},"atlas-v","launcher",{"id":2,"role":43},"spacecraft",{"launch":45,"cruise":51,"arrival":55,"totals":63,"events":67,"interplanetary_profile":107},{"vehicle_stage":46,"c3_km2_s2":47,"declination_deg":48,"mass_at_tli_kg":49,"source":50},"Centaur upper stage (Atlas V 541)",14.79,16.7,4060,"NASA Mars 2020 Press Kit (2020-07); ULA Atlas V 541 mission overview",{"tcm_count":52,"peak_heliocentric_speed_km_s":53,"source":54},5,33.5,"JPL Mars 2020 EDL Reconstruction (2021)",{"v_infinity_km_s":56,"entry_velocity_km_s":57,"periapsis_km":58,"inclination_deg":58,"orbit_insertion_dv_km_s":58,"source":59,"edl_system":60,"edl_duration_s":61,"touchdown_velocity_ms":62},2.4,5.334,null,"NASA Mars 2020 Press Kit (2021-02); JPL Mars 2020 EDL Telemetry","skycrane",405,0.75,{"total_dv_km_s":64,"tli_or_tmi_dv_km_s":65,"source":66},6.1,3.85,"computed from Mars 2020 ∆v ledger (NASA Press Kit, 2020-07)",[68,73,78,83,87,90,94,98,102],{"met_days":69,"type":70,"label":71,"description":72},0,"launch","Launch — Atlas V 541","Cape Canaveral, 2020-07-30. Mars 2020 carries Perseverance — a near-identical chassis to Curiosity but with a sample-caching coring system and the Ingenuity helicopter strapped under the belly. Designed to land in Jezero Crater, a 3.5-Gyr-old river delta sediment trap chosen specifically for organic-preservation potential.",{"met_days":74,"type":75,"label":76,"description":77},0.005,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-Mars injection","Centaur upper stage burn at T+57 minutes sends Perseverance + Ingenuity on a 7-month transfer.",{"met_days":79,"type":80,"label":81,"description":82},15,"tcm","TCM-1","First post-TMI cleanup burn.",{"met_days":84,"type":80,"label":85,"description":86},40.6,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":88,"type":80,"label":89,"description":86},60,"TCM-3",{"met_days":91,"type":80,"label":92,"description":93},140,"TCM-4","Approach-phase adjustment.",{"met_days":95,"type":80,"label":96,"description":97},180,"TCM-5 — final pre-EDL burn","Tightens approach targeting for the Jezero EDL ellipse.",{"met_days":15,"type":99,"label":100,"description":101},"arrival","Mars approach + cruise-stage separation","2021-02-18. 10 minutes before atmospheric entry, the cruise stage jettisons; the backshell + descent stage + rover enters Mars's atmosphere at 5.4 km/s.",{"met_days":103,"type":104,"label":105,"description":106},203.005,"edl_or_oi","Mars EDL — sky-crane landing in Jezero Crater","\"Seven minutes of terror\", same architecture as Curiosity but adding Terrain-Relative Navigatio